Final Fantasy 15 director Hajime Tabata  revealed a whole lot more about the  upcoming JRPG in an interview with  French cyclist video chill Shockers  translated the interview and dug up a  number of interesting bits and pieces  including that the Final Fantasy 15 team  consists of about 300 people worldwide  Tabata also said the game has just  entered the localization phase of  development and they're currently  working to balance different  environments experience games and  weapons as well as optimizing the frame  rate he said this time around there will  be less cinematic cutscenes than in  previous Final Fantasy games but they  intend to put more cinematic elements  into the actual game on the topic of  flying cars Tabata explained that you  need to customize the regalia to make it  fly and then all you need to do is hit a  button to get it airborne just like in  the trailer featured at squares  uncovered event Tabata added that they  will be announcing DLC plans for Final  Fantasy 15 this summer and he's  interested in doing a PC version once  the console version is out he said he  hopes to create a version of 15 which is  even more technically elaborate and that  incorporates the features they couldn't  include due to current technical  limitations Tabata did emphasize that  this wouldn't be a simple port of the  console version and they would  essentially need to begin almost from  scratch let me know in the comments what  you think about the latest on Final  Fantasy 15 and for everything else that  matters in gaming head to GameSpot calm
 

